<div id="recipe-82362-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82362-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82362"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82362-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Cut onions in half lengthwise, remove the skins, and slice thinly into half-moon shapes. Transfer to a medium bowl.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82362-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Add the olive oil, lemon juice, Kosher salt, sumac, and Aleppo pepper.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Two images side by side showing onions being thinly sliced and onions in a bowl garnished with sumac." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Turkish-onion-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82362-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Using your hands, gently massage the onions for 1&ndash;2 minutes until they soften slightly and absorb the seasonings.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82362-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Add the parsley and toss to combine.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing sumac onions massaged and then garnished with parsley." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/How-to-make-sumac-onions.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-82362-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><span style="font-weight: 400"><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe makes &frac12; to &frac34; of sumac onions, which would be ideal for serving 4 adults. The nutritional values below are per serving.</span></li>
<li><strong>Onions:</strong> While the traditional recipe is made with red onions, in a pinch, you can use white onions, but keep in mind that the flavor profile will be slightly different.</li>
<li><strong>Make Ahead:</strong> These onions get even better as they sit. You can prepare them 2-3 days in advance and store them in an airtight container or jar in the fridge.</li>
<li><strong>Storage:</strong> Store leftovers in the fridge for up to 4 days. <span style="font-weight: 400">Just give them a quick stir before serving to mix the seasonings back in.</span></li>
<li><strong>Freezing:</strong> Not recommended, as the onions lose their crisp texture once thawed. For the best flavor and crunch, enjoy them fresh.</li>
</ul></div></div>
